      "heading": "What paperless really means",
      "html": "<p>A PDF form filled in at a desk after the job is the same process with a new output. Paperless means you record the finding when the fault is in front of you. The photo is attached there. The voice note is said there. Nothing is rebuilt from memory two hours later.</p><p>A record made on the spot is more accurate. And the evening write-up goes away. Ask one question of any tool: can I finish it on site, or does it just make a PDF at a desk?</p>"
